These cached contexts were computed using the official external Wan UMT5-XXL
encoder and tokenizer from Wan-AI/Wan2.1-T2V-1.3B, revision
37ec512624d61f7aa208f7ea8140a131f93afc9a, distributed under Apache-2.0.
The encoder checkpoint is not included. The tensors are actual encoder outputs
for the two recorded prompts, not pretrained encoder parameters or an original
Worldline text model.

The native negative text is copied verbatim from the Alibaba Wan Team's shared
configuration at Wan-Video/Wan2.1 revision
9737cba9c1c3c4d04b33fcad41c111989865d315, under Apache-2.0. Its original copyright
header, source snapshot, hash and license are retained in ../native-source/.
The unchanged positive text was authored for the Worldline Atrium experiment.

Selected Wan/minWM encoder source retains its separate attribution and license
copies in ../vendor/ and ../NOTICE. A copy of Apache-2.0 accompanies these
cached outputs. The original two-prompt cache remains separately in ../results/.
